$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4,4'''-Dimethyl-[1,1':4',1'':4'',1'''-quaterphenyl]-2''-yl)(phenyl)methanone
(3f): A mixture of 2c (2.08 g, 5 mmol), p-tolylboronic acid (1.63 g, 12
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (0.35 g, 0.3 mmol), and potassium carbonate (2.76 g, 20
mmol) in 200 mL of toluene/ethanol/water (8/1/1 v/v/v) was heated to
reflux for 12 h under nitrogen. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, poured into water, and extracted twice with dichloromethane.
The combined organic layers were washed with saturated brine solution and
water, and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After filtration and
solvent evaporation, the residue was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography using hexane/dichloromethane as eluent. White solid, yield
82% (1.80 g). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.80 (dd, J = 8.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H),
7.74-7.72 (m, 3H), 7.59 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.56-7.55 (m, 2H), 7.44-7.39
(m, 5H), 7.36-7.34 (m, 2H), 7.30-7.26 (m, 4H), 7.20 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H),
2.40 (s, 3H), 2.37 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 198.8, 140.0,
