$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General reaction procedure of Suzuki coupling reaction on
dichloromethylene derivatives (4, 13 and 26-28) with arylboronic acids
Dichloromethylene derivative (1.0 mmol), aryl-boronic acid (2.5 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (30 mg) and PPh3 (20 mg), potassium carbonate (1.38 g, 10.0
mmol) and benzyltriethyl ammonium chloride (0.5 g, 2.2 mmol) were taken
in a mixture of toluene (20 ml) and water (10 ml). The reaction mixture
was heated at 110 ºC for 24 h in nitrogen atmosphere. On completion of
reaction the mixture was cooled, and toluene layer was separated. On
removal of toluene the product was purified by column chromatography
using dichloromethane/hexane as eluent. Preparation of
6-(diphenylmethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (5) According to general
reaction procedure, 6-(dichloromethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (4) (0.32 g,
1.0 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (0.26 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted. Product
as light-yellow solid. Yield: 0.32 g, 80%. Mp: 235 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz) δ: 7.90 (s, 4H), 7.74-7.72 (m, 2H), 7.48 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
7.25-7.13 (m, 12H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 145.7, 144.2, 133.5,
133.2, 130.9 129.9, 129.0, 128.8, 128.6, 128.0, 127.2, 126.7, 126.4,
126.2, 125.2. MALDI-TOF MS: calculated for [C32H20]+: 404.1559, found:
404.1550.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
